      "source": [
        "# Multi-Session Handoff Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A loader that gathers state, verdict, review, and feedback into a single `WorkbenchSnapshot`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A `generate_handoff(snapshot) -> (markdown, payload)` function."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A filter that picks the last K feedback entries plus all non-zero exits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A demo run that writes `handoff.md` and `handoff.json` next to the script."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: a printed handoff body, plus both files on disk."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add an `assumptions_to_validate` field that surfaces every assumption the builder logged but the reviewer did not score above 1.\n2. Trim the feedback summary differently for failing runs versus passing ones. Defend the asymmetry.\n3. Include a \"questions for the human\" list. What is the threshold for a question to make it into the packet versus into a chat message?\n4. Make the generator idempotent: running it twice produces the same packet. What needs to be stable for that to hold?\n5. Add a \"next session prereqs\" section listing exactly the artifacts the next session must load before acting."
      ]
    }
  ],
